Z||000014||bHooper||04-28-2001||08:26 PM||||the FIA (the body that rules <B>ALL</B> auto racing... even neckar) will allow CART to run outside of the North America, if they run on ovals only (Austrailia being the exception).  <BR>thats kind of ironic, considering that F1, now race's here on a road course!<P>as for Villeneuve, don't forget, he raced CART until the end of the '95 season.  <P>and it is, afterall, a movie.  i saw some of the "making of the movie" shows, and there are far too many crash's, and explosions... but that's what sells movies.  no one wants to go to a movie, for 2.5 hours and see cars go around a track with nothing happening!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's<BR>and spellcheck crash's windows<BR>Poly Bushings<BR>Accel Coil||||reg||1
