Z||000020||Cameron||04-29-2001||04:45 PM||||Well I would have to agree, it wasn't as good as gone in 60 seconds.  But it was still a good movie.  What can you expect, the actors weren't as good.  I liked the racing scenes however.  You can't judge a movie like this on it's plot.  It has none to speak of.  Well it does but it pretty much sucks.  I just loved the racing scenes and there were a couple sweet crashes.<P>FieroLisa - Dang that is a dilema.  I know what you should do.  Pick them up, throw them in the car, and drag them into the theater to watch the movie.  Ok well maybe not, but that would work.  Aside from that ... you got a problem.  Going by yourself would suck.  I hate going to movies alone it really sucks.<P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||KnightRyder31||04-29-2001||08:45 PM||||Didn't like it. I left early.<BR>When does Fast And Furious come out?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Cheever2||04-29-2001||08:51 PM||||I liked it a lot.  Much better than the critics led me to believe, as usual.  I even liked it better than the other Forum reviews so far.  Not a great movie, no, but I was very impressed with the shots they got and the overall look of the close racing scenes.  I can forgive the things that were definitely not realistic, like the crashes that went WAY up in the air, and the chase through the city streets.  The only thing I didn't like was the countless times they showed a foot stomping on the accelerator, often just for effect, when the driver's foot should have already been to the floor.  They didn't have to show that each and every time one car passed another.  The story was silly, as someone already mentioned, but not as silly as Days of Thunder.  I just didn't believe that the young driver would be so close to the championship if he didn't already know what it took to be a winner, which is what Stallone was there to teach him.<P>BTW, I LIKE clean-cut and boy-scout.  It should have been MORE like that, in my opinion.  But I will let my teenage boys see it, if they want to.  I wouldn't mind seeing it again, that's for sure.<BR>||||reg||14
